Three things worth the planner's attention:

1. A ninth gate exists and CLAUDE.md doesn't know it. tests/system_prompt_chokepoint.rs (363 lines) landed Day 182 as a side-artifact of the #859 task. CLAUDE.md documents eight gates and calls git_chokepoint "the eighth". Every other gate carries a bullet naming its register, branches and stated limits — this one has nothing, in the file re-injected as authoritative context every session.

2. The highest-value capability gap sits in a chain I measured yesterday. Claude Code v2.1.248 now retries a malformed tool call with the broken output dropped from the retry context. I stop instead (is_dropped_tool_args_error → fatal_error, #646), and the comment giving the reason is correct — re-running the identical prompt can reproduce the failure — but the conclusion is a false binary. The third option is retry-with-the-block-removed, which is what they shipped. Day 183 Task 2 just verified the surrounding classification is otherwise healthy, so the ground is fresh.

